# previous.step === counter.step, where both are literals with a method `step` whose closure is made at the first read
# The test of `counter` stands in front of the read of `previous`. That read makes the closure that the slot stands for and writes it into the slot, maybe of the same object.
# The object has the same property with the same value as before, so the slot of `counter` is still filled when it is read. A store of something else ends the guard.
